WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:08.879
The guests at Fred's party were still laughing at the idea of Ebenezer Scrooge as a scary beast.

2
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.028
At last Fred stopped laughing and managed to speak again.

3
00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:16.905
"You're wrong, my dear sister-in-law," Fred said.

4
00:00:16.906 --> 00:00:21.551
"I was thinking of a bear , not my uncle

5
00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:26.469
Scrooge." "Well, your uncle fits just as well," Mary

6
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:34.228
said. "Indeed, I can't imagine a more savage, growling, frightening beast than Mr.

7
00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:41.385
Scrooge!" Scrooge turned to the spirit. "I hope it's time to leave this dreadful

8
00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:46.873
scene." The spirit nodded and then whisked him away

9
00:00:46.874 --> 00:00:51.727
again. This time they arrived in a much larger, finer house than Fred's

10
00:00:51.728 --> 00:00:55.648
home. A Christmas party was going on here

11
00:00:55.649 --> 00:01:02.833
too. However, this celebration was taking place in a grand ballroom with two

12
00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:09.643
musicians. The gentlemen were dressed in their finest suits, and all the women wore lovely, formal

13
00:01:09.644 --> 00:01:17.876
dresses. "Oh, I know that fellow there," Scrooge said, recognizing a business acquaintance among the

14
00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:23.872
crowd. "Oh! And that tall gentleman over there

15
00:01:23.873 --> 00:01:29.940
too." Looking around more closely, he realized he knew many of the men gathered in the

16
00:01:29.941 --> 00:01:35.122
ballroom. They were all of the most successful businessmen in London, in fact.

17
00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:39.960
"But what is this place, spirit?" Scrooge asked.

18
00:01:39.961 --> 00:01:45.507
"Why are all these people gathered here together?"

19
00:01:45.508 --> 00:01:50.101
The spirit drifted closer to one small group of men.

20
00:01:50.102 --> 00:01:54.963
Scrooge followed the spirit and listened to the men's conversation.

21
00:01:54.964 --> 00:02:01.243
"I congratulate you on hosting another splendid holiday celebration, Cavendish," a man said.

22
00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:04.583
He lifted his glass to Mr. Cavendish.

23
00:02:04.584 --> 00:02:09.813
"Yes, all of London's most important businessmen are here!" another man added.

24
00:02:09.814 --> 00:02:13.244
"And we're having a wonderful time."

25
00:02:13.245 --> 00:02:20.936
A third man chuckled. " Nearly everyone is here, you

26
00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:26.820
mean. I don't see old Ebenezer Scrooge enjoying himself on the dance

27
00:02:26.821 --> 00:02:31.773
floor. Did you, er, forget to invite him again,

28
00:02:31.774 --> 00:02:38.567
Cavendish?" "Oh, what a shame." Cavendish smirked and tapped his own head

29
00:02:38.568 --> 00:02:43.306
playfully. "I can't imagine how the most important guest slipped my

30
00:02:43.307 --> 00:02:50.091
mind. After all, the old boy is the life of the party everywhere he goes, isn't

31
00:02:50.092 --> 00:02:54.971
he?" At that, the businessmen all laughed

32
00:02:54.972 --> 00:03:01.909
loudly. Scrooge scowled. "How dare they speak of me this way!" he

33
00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.507
said. "I've never done anything to harm

34
00:03:05.508 --> 00:03:10.359
them. And yet here they are mocking and degrading me without

35
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.575
mercy!" The spirit was silent for a

36
00:03:14.576 --> 00:03:20.259
moment. "It's true that you've done nothing to harm them," he finally

37
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:25.036
said. "Yet, you've done nothing to help them

38
00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.713
either." He gestured at one of the

39
00:03:27.714 --> 00:03:33.339
men. "When Mr. Aston lost his wife last year, did you attend the

40
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:41.138
funeral? When Mr. Cavendish needed a loan for his newest business, did you step up and offer to help

41
00:03:41.139 --> 00:03:44.777
him?" "Of course not!" Scrooge

42
00:03:44.778 --> 00:03:48.302
snapped. "Those things had nothing to do with

43
00:03:48.303 --> 00:03:52.019
me. However, my business is successful

44
00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.710
too. These men could include me in their

45
00:03:56.711 --> 00:04:02.218
gatherings." "If you say so." The spirit

46
00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:08.776
shrugged. "However, you might say that their parties and celebrations have nothing to do with you

47
00:04:08.777 --> 00:04:15.284
either. If you can't spare a thought for their troubles, why do you expect them to spare any thoughts of

48
00:04:15.285 --> 00:04:19.880
you? Or invite you to their social

49
00:04:19.881 --> 00:04:24.832
events?" Scrooge grunted. He couldn't argue with the spirit's

50
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:31.214
logic. And before this strange night, he wouldn't have cared one bit about attending this

51
00:04:31.215 --> 00:04:38.960
party. "I'm not that earnest young man dancing with his friends at Fezziwig's," Scrooge said to the spirit.

52
00:04:38.961 --> 00:04:45.498
"Not anymore. I have more important things to occupy my thoughts."

53
00:04:45.499 --> 00:04:49.680
Just then something flashed in his mind.

54
00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:59.495
"Although, I must admit, sometimes I do think of that silly fellow Dick Wilkins from Fezziwig's business.

55
00:04:59.496 --> 00:05:03.533
I wonder what became of him."

56
00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.619
The spirit snapped his fingers.

57
00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:12.231
The grand ballroom disappeared, replaced by a modest tailor's shop.

58
00:05:12.232 --> 00:05:15.359
Scrooge watched as the tailor bent over a garment.

59
00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.839
He seemed to be mending a jacket while its owner, a young man, waited.

60
00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.619
"Thank you so much for opening your shop on Christmas," the young man said.

61
00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.666
"It's so very kind of you.

62
00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:34.371
I was afraid to show up for Christmas dinner at my father-in-law's house with a rip in my coat.

63
00:05:34.372 --> 00:05:38.059
My wife would faint from embarrassment!"

64
00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.292
"I'm happy to do it, Mr. Perry.

65
00:05:41.293 --> 00:05:49.119
After all, my own wife would be horrified if I turned away someone in need at Christmastime."

66
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.783
The tailor looked up and smiled around a mouthful of pins.

67
00:05:53.784 --> 00:05:57.526
That was when Scrooge recognized him.

68
00:05:57.527 --> 00:06:01.979
"Why, that's him, spirit!" Scrooge said.

69
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:07.938
"It's Dick Wilkins!"

